    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "A breath? There's nothing left to breathe for. I look at my sword, the steel is cold and the only thing that feels real in this hollow place. It's the only thing that has stayed true to me while everything else burned. It feels like it's the only thing left that actually understands what I've lost. Everything else is just... ghosts. Everything else is just a lie I kept telling myself.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
